~ start
PILI: Eat up, children. The wind is getting a bit chilly tonight so make sure you finish all your hot soup.

Today's meal is my favorite sinigang made by Nanay! I already can smell exactly how sour the soup is just by looking at it. Yum!

VALERIE: Dodong, stop chewing with your mouth open. And Noni, sit properly or you're going to spill your broth everywhere. I'm not cleaning up after you tonight.

DODONG: Look, Noni! I bet you I can swallow this whole fish tail in one bite! 

NONI: No, kuya! Don't do it!

KIKI: Fish! Nom-nom..

VALERIE: Hey! Stop playing with your food! Both of you! This isn't a playground. Look at Ollie. At least someone in this house knows how to sit quietly and behave like a good child. Nanay, tell them to stop! 

PILI: Valerie, lower your voice. Let them eat. But Dodong, Noni, listen to your Ate. Don't be so stubborn, okay? It's bad to play with our blessings. 

DODONG: Ate Valerie is just being a bossy police officer again. Weee-wooo-weee-wooo!

VALERIE: Tatay, see? They never listen to me! I'm just trying to keep the table clean so Nanay doesn't have to work extra hard and they just—

The entire table instantly goes quiet as Tatay sets his glass down with a heavy thud. I look down at my plate waiting for Tatay to look scary and scold us. To my surprise, he wasn’t angry. Instead, I saw a happy smile crack across his tired face. 

ERNESTO: Alright, alright, that's enough bickering. We are here to eat, not to fight. Especially not tonight. We have a lot to be happy about.

PILI: That's right. It's November 6 already. In just two days, it’s going to be our Ollie's birthday!

NONI: Yay! Kuya Ollie’s birthday!

VALERIE: Noni, quiet down, let Tatay speak first. But... can we, Nay? I want to help you bake a chocolate cake for Ollie on Friday.

PILI: We will see, anak. You know things have been tight this month…

ERNESTO: Actually, Pili... we don't have to worry about that anymore. 
ERNESTO: The boss from Millgate called me this afternoon. They want to buy our entire copra harvest this month and they are paying a higher price than any of the middlemen!

NONI: Really, Tay?! The big company?

DODONG: Yes! That means we can finally fix our backyard! And maybe get the basketball I wanted!

KIKI: Yaaaay!

VALERIE: Oh my gosh, Tay! Really?! That means we can buy our school supplies for next term, right? 
VALERIE: And I can help Nanay budget for the groceries. 
VALERIE: Ollie, we can definitely prepare a birthday party for you now!

PILI: Salamat sa Diyos, Ernesto. This is a true blessing from heaven. We can finally pay off everything we owe. And also like Valerie said, we can finally celebrate Ollie's 8th birthday properly.

Wow! Millgate must be a magical place. If they give Tatay lots of coins, that means we'll get rich! I can finally buy toys without Tatay or Nanay having to work until their bones ache. 

Maybe my birthday won't feel like a burden this year. 

With this big deal, nothing bad can ever happen to us. 

NONI: Kuya Ollie. On your birthday, I'll give you my best drawing as a present! 

DODONG: We should celebrate! Kuya Andrei said the Millgate trucks are massive. I want to watch them load up all our coconuts! 

VALERIE: See, Ollie? You don't have to look so worried anymore. Eat more! We're going to be totally fine. Your birthday is going to be perfect.

OLLIE: Thank you, Ate.

Ate Valerie is right. Nothing bad can ever- BZZZZT.

=> END